      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The borough once produced millions of cigars per month, about 10% of U.S. output, and still raises a cigar every New Year's Eve.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Lion%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Red Lion Area Historical Society Museum showcases the town’s cigar‑making heritage and community traditions.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.atlasvanlines.com/city-guides/red-lion-pa",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Red Lion was a main stop on the historic Maryland and Pennsylvania Railroad, known locally as the “Ma & Pa” Railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Lion%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town’s furniture industry shifted to kitchen cabinet production and retail fixtures over the last 40 years.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Lion%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
